--- field object.account.sid
type: bin.sid

The SID of the account a record is about: a principal a principal source
holds, whose credential was checked or changed, or which was created,
deleted or modified. The SID, never the name: an account can be renamed,
and a record that named it would then describe someone else.

Not `object.token.sid`, which is the user of a token. A token speaks for
an account, but an account changed while nobody is signed in has no token
to name it by.

--- field object.group.sid
type: bin.sid

The SID of the group a record is about: one a principal source created or
deleted, or whose membership it changed. It may be a group of the source's
own domain or a well-known one such as `BUILTIN\Administrators`, which a
local source records memberships of.

--- event lpsd.credential.verified
tier: standard
gating: none — every credential lpsd checks for a logon is recorded
cardinality: once per logon lpsd decides; probing which SSH keys an account would accept writes none

The record that lpsd checked a credential for a logon authd relayed to it,
and what it found. It says what the wire must not: authd and the
originator are told only "authentication failed" whether the account does
not exist or the credential was wrong, and `outcome.reason` here tells
them apart for whoever may read the audit trail.

The account is named by SID when it exists. The name the caller typed is
never recorded, so a failure against a name lpsd does not hold carries no
account at all; `authd.logon.attempted` is the same logon as the authority
saw it.

Standard rather than essential because a machine exposed to a network can
be asked to check credentials far more often than it signs anyone in.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  lpsd itself, the principal that checked the credential: the user SID of
  lpsd's own token, which is its service account.
field: object.account.sid                   optional
  The account the credential was checked for. Absent when lpsd holds no
  account by the name it was asked about.
field: operation.name                       required
  values: password | ssh-key | none
  closed: false
  What was checked. `none` is an account whose policy is that it signs in
  with no credential, asserted without asking for one.
field: outcome.success                      required
  True when lpsd told authd who the principal is.
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: no-such-account | wrong-credential | disabled | not-permitted
  closed: false
  `not-permitted` is an account whose credential policy does not allow
  the kind of credential offered, or a key the account does not hold.

--- event lpsd.credential.changed
tier: essential
gating: none — every change of an account's own credential is recorded, and every refusal once the account is known
cardinality: once per change conversation that reaches the account

The record that a principal changed their own password, or added or
removed one of their own SSH keys, through authd (PSPU §2.21, §2.23), or
tried to and was refused. A change an administrator makes with `lps` is
`lpsd.account.modified`.

Essential because a changed credential is how an account changes hands,
and it is rare.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  The principal that asked, as authd vouched for them from their token.
  The same SID as `object.account.sid`: only one's own credential can be
  changed this way.
field: object.account.sid                   required
field: operation.name                       required
  values: password | ssh-key-added | ssh-key-removed
  closed: false
field: outcome.success                      required
  True once the change is durable.
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: no-such-account | disabled | no-credential | wrong-credential | superseded | rejected | conversation-limit | not-saved
  closed: false
  `no-credential` is an account with no password to prove itself with;
  `superseded` a password that changed between the rounds of the
  conversation; `rejected` a new password or key the store refused;
  `conversation-limit` too many unusable new passwords; `not-saved` a
  change the store could not make durable, so it was not applied.

--- event lpsd.account.created
tier: essential
gating: none — every request to create an account is recorded
cardinality: once per request

The record that an administrator created a local account with `lps`, or
tried to. The first account on a new machine is created this way too, by
the boot-time service that provisions it.

Essential because a new account is a new way in, and it is rare.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  The administrator: the user SID of the token that asked.
field: object.account.sid                   when outcome.success == true
  The new account.
field: outcome.success                      required
  True once the account is durable.
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: not-found | exists | invalid | internal | not-saved
  closed: false
  The failure `lps` was told: `not-found` names a group that does not
  exist, `exists` an account name already in use, `invalid` a value the
  store refuses, `not-saved` a change that could not be made durable.

--- event lpsd.account.deleted
tier: essential
gating: none — every request to delete an account is recorded
cardinality: once per request

The record that an administrator deleted a local account with `lps`, or
tried to.

Essential because deleting an account is irreversible and rare: its SID is
never issued again, and every descriptor naming it names nobody.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  The administrator.
field: object.account.sid                   optional
  The account. Absent when no account had the name asked for.
field: outcome.success                      required
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: not-found | invalid | internal | not-saved
  closed: false
  `invalid` is a deletion the store refuses, such as of the last
  administrator.

--- event lpsd.account.modified
tier: essential
gating: none — every administrative change to an account, and every change of one's own display name, is recorded; a request that changes nothing is not
cardinality: once per request that changes something or fails

The record that an account was changed: by an administrator with `lps`,
or by the principal themselves where the self socket allows it. Which
change it was is `operation.name`.

A request that would leave the account as it was, such as enabling an
enabled account, changes nothing and writes no record.

Essential because an account's settings decide who can sign in and as
what, and they change rarely.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  The principal that asked: an administrator, or the account itself for
  `set-display-name`.
field: object.account.sid                   optional
  The account changed. Absent when no account had the name asked for.
field: object.group.sid                     optional
  For `set-primary-group`, the group made the account's primary group.
field: operation.name                       required
  values: set-enabled | set-password | set-profile | set-display-name | set-primary-group | set-claim | remove-claim | rename | set-logon-types | key-add | key-remove | set-credential-policy
  closed: false
  The change, as `lps` names its command. `set-display-name` is the
  principal's own, through the self socket.
field: outcome.success                      required
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: not-found | exists | invalid | internal | denied | not-saved
  closed: false
  `denied` is a disabled account changing its own display name.

--- event lpsd.group.created
tier: essential
gating: none — every request to create a group is recorded
cardinality: once per request

The record that an administrator created a local group with `lps`, or
tried to.

Essential because groups are what descriptors grant to, and they are
created rarely.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  The administrator.
field: object.group.sid                     when outcome.success == true
  The new group.
field: outcome.success                      required
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: exists | invalid | internal | not-saved
  closed: false

--- event lpsd.group.deleted
tier: essential
gating: none — every request to delete a group is recorded
cardinality: once per request

The record that an administrator deleted a local group with `lps`, or
tried to.

Essential because deleting a group removes every grant made to it, and it
is rare.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  The administrator.
field: object.group.sid                     optional
  The group. Absent when no group had the name asked for.
field: outcome.success                      required
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: not-found | invalid | internal | not-saved
  closed: false

--- event lpsd.group.member.added
tier: essential
gating: none — every request to add a membership is recorded; one that already held is not
cardinality: once per request that changes something or fails

The record that an administrator added an account to a group with `lps`,
or tried to. The group may be a well-known one: adding an account to
`BUILTIN\Administrators` is recorded here.

Essential because a membership is a grant of everything granted to the
group, and memberships change rarely.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  The administrator.
field: object.account.sid                   optional
  The account. Absent when no account had the name asked for.
field: object.group.sid                     optional
  The group. Absent when no group had the name asked for.
field: outcome.success                      required
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: not-found | invalid | internal | not-saved
  closed: false

--- event lpsd.group.member.removed
tier: essential
gating: none — every request to remove a membership is recorded; one that did not hold is not
cardinality: once per request that changes something or fails

The record that an administrator removed an account from a group with
`lps`, or tried to.

Essential for the reason `lpsd.group.member.added` is: a membership is a
grant, and taking one away is as much an access change as giving it.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  The administrator.
field: object.account.sid                   optional
  The account. Absent when no account had the name asked for.
field: object.group.sid                     optional
  The group. Absent when no group had the name asked for.
field: outcome.success                      required
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: not-found | invalid | internal | not-saved
  closed: false
  `invalid` includes removing the last administrator from
  `BUILTIN\Administrators`.
